From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 14:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mac80211_hwsim: reserve headroom for software encryption

mac80211_hwsim accepts CCMP and GCMP keys in mac80211_hwsim_set_key()
and encrypts unicast data frames itself in mac80211_hwsim_tx(), through
ieee80211_encrypt_tx_skb(). It asks mac80211 to reserve tailroom for the
MIC, but not headroom for the CCMP or GCMP header.

For a hardware key without IEEE80211_KEY_FLAG_GENERATE_IV or
IEEE80211_KEY_FLAG_PUT_IV_SPACE, ieee80211_xmit_fast() resizes the frame
with ENCRYPT_NO and reserves only the 802.11 header and
hw.extra_tx_headroom. A locally generated frame usually has room to
spare, but a frame forwarded from a bridge can arrive with none. The
room check in ccmp_encrypt_skb() then warns, ieee80211_encrypt_tx_skb()
returns an error and the frame is freed. An access point that bridges
traffic to its clients sends no downlink unicast data at all.

Reserve the header as driver headroom. IEEE80211_CCMP_HDR_LEN,
IEEE80211_CCMP_256_HDR_LEN and IEEE80211_GCMP_HDR_LEN are all 8 bytes.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/virtual/mac80211_hwsim_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/virtual/mac80211_hwsim_main.c
@@ -5913,6 +5913,7 @@ static int mac80211_hwsim_new_radio(stru
 
 	hw->queues = 5;
 	hw->offchannel_tx_hw_queue = 4;
+	hw->extra_tx_headroom = IEEE80211_CCMP_HDR_LEN;
 
 	ieee80211_hw_set(hw, SUPPORT_FAST_XMIT);
 	ieee80211_hw_set(hw, CHANCTX_STA_CSA);
